// A bill of sale for Grace Tanaka's 2015 Corolla, sold to Leo Varga (bill-of-sale.md).
Document "bill-of-sale.md"

Fact person Identified by Grace, Leo
Placeholder seller For person
Placeholder buyer For person
Fact car Identified by Corolla
Fact usd Identified by Money(USD, 2)
Param price : Money(USD, 2) = 650000

// 1 and 2.1. Payment and delivery; ownership passes when both are done
Function owner Identified by car * person
Fact paid Identified by seller * buyer * car
Fact delivered Identified by seller * buyer * car
Act pay Actor buyer Recipient seller Related to car, usd
  Holds when True
  Valid when usd == price
  Creates paid(), owner(car, buyer) When delivered() && owner(car, seller)
Act deliver Actor seller Recipient buyer Related to car
  Holds when owner(car, seller)
  Creates delivered(), owner(car, buyer) When paid() && owner(car, seller)

// 2.2 The signed title, within five days
Fact title-handed Identified by seller * buyer * car
Duty title-due Holder seller Claimant buyer Related to car
  Holds when paid() && delivered() && owner(car, buyer) && Not(title-handed())
  Due within 5
Act hand-over-title Actor seller Recipient buyer Related to car
  Holds when True
  Creates title-handed()

// 3. Ownership, liens, the odometer: the buyer may cancel and is refunded in ten days
Evidenced Fact lien Identified by car
Evidenced Fact knew-reading-wrong Identified by seller * car
Fact cancelled Identified by seller * buyer * car
Power cancel Actor buyer Recipient seller Related to car
  Holds when True
  Valid when paid() && Not(cancelled())
    && ((Not(owner(car, seller)) && Not(owner(car, buyer))) || lien() || knew-reading-wrong())
  Creates cancelled(), owner(car, seller) When owner(car, buyer)
Duty refund-due Holder seller Claimant buyer Related to car
  Due within 10
  Created by cancel
  Terminated by refund
Act refund Actor seller Recipient buyer Related to car

// 4. As is, unless the seller knew of the defect and concealed it
Fact defect
Evidenced Fact known Identified by defect
Fact disclosed Identified by defect
Act disclose Actor seller Recipient buyer Related to defect
  Holds when True
  Creates disclosed()
Immunity as-is Holder seller Related to defect Against demand-repair
  Holds when True
  Unless known() && Not(disclosed())
Act demand-repair Actor buyer Recipient seller Related to car, defect
  Holds when delivered()
Duty repair-due Holder seller Claimant buyer Related to car, defect
  Due within 30
  Created by demand-repair
  Terminated by pay-for-repair
Act pay-for-repair Actor seller Recipient buyer Related to car, defect

Clause 1.1 Approved "a13f8589eb42df13f6f1af48d67cffcb6bf70235b66cc7bd558f784c100f7a0b"
  Norm "Grace Tanaka, the seller, sells her 2015 Corolla to Leo Varga, the buyer, for six thousand five hundred dollars." => pay, deliver
Clause 2.1 Approved "3a3953d55ea771e87726ef1ee4585698ff06c66891ed366e192e67d54c39fd9f"
  Norm "Ownership of the car passes to the buyer when the buyer has paid the price and the seller has delivered the car." => pay, deliver
  Norm " A seller passes only the ownership she has." => pay, deliver
Clause 2.2 Approved "abdd88990260b4069415e7c9817db3057820f41a94ef0f3c9e53edecfd2261db"
  Norm "The seller hands the signed certificate of title to the buyer within five days after ownership passes." => title-due, hand-over-title
Clause 3.1 Approved "11235defae0eaba3550ee36d1a22189213a237abfa6d1aedbd32ca1c0b9b580a"
  Norm "The seller warrants that she owns the car and that there is no lien on it." => deliver, cancel
Clause 3.2 Approved "0002748988386efd48cc4241338c481de3baa58801a9daf81ac16d552b05d765"
  Definition "The seller states that the odometer reads 84,210 miles and that she knows of no reason why that is not the distance the car has travelled."
Clause 3.3 Approved "ba52354ecf677c328b68f55d6e4f5d982fe9fd62266b412cee80515426ebc49c"
  Norm "If the seller did not own the car, or there is a lien on it, or the seller knew the odometer reading was wrong, the buyer may cancel the sale." => cancel
  Norm " The car then goes back to the seller, and the seller refunds the price within ten days after the cancellation." => cancel, refund-due, refund
Clause 4.1 Approved "fdd583ee979661838e426f4f714e175e7205379baa89427e72ee868fbb62a918"
  Norm "The car is sold as is. The seller gives no warranty of its condition, and the buyer has no claim against the seller for a defect." => as-is, demand-repair
Clause 4.2 Approved "9b81ea4bcf1f878b70699bc4886757f468885bee9834e7cc2b0206b297ce2bf5"
  Norm "That does not protect a seller who knew of a defect and concealed it from the buyer." => as-is, disclose
  Norm " The seller pays for the repair of such a defect within thirty days after the buyer demands it." => demand-repair, repair-due, pay-for-repair
.
